realsense-ros 4.59.2 on ROS Lyrical: do not force-load ROS's libfastdds (Fast DDS 3.x) ahead of
librealsense, whose realdds has Fast DDS 2.10 built in; with it the node segfaults at start (2026-11-15).

diff --git a/realsense2_camera/CMakeLists.txt b/realsense2_camera/CMakeLists.txt
index b6eb588..6500f1d 100644
--- a/realsense2_camera/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/realsense2_camera/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -366,7 +366,10 @@ target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME}
 # configure time, find_library returns NOTFOUND and the workaround silently
 # no-ops — users on Cyclone/Zenoh with a non-DDS librealsense (the common
 # case) aren't forced to install FastDDS via rosdep.
-if(fastcdr_FOUND AND UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
+# Not on Lyrical: there libfastdds is Fast DDS 3.x, while librealsense's realdds carries its own
+# Fast DDS 2.10 statically. Forcing 3.x to load first makes realdds resolve shared symbol names
+# (eprosima::fastdds::dds::...) into 3.x: the node segfaults at start (rover, 2026-11-15).
+if(fastcdr_FOUND AND UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT "$ENV{ROS_DISTRO}" STREQUAL "lyrical")
   # Humble and Jazzy still ship the library as libfastrtps.so; it was renamed
   # to libfastdds.so in Kilted. find_library returns the first match, so
   # try fastdds first (Kilted/Lyrical/Rolling), fall through to fastrtps
